    "body": "claimed: tbrasselle · 2026-11-10T01:27Z · branch issue/622-viewcube-roll-snap · plan: at an exact Z pole (`abs(d.z) = 1` in `Camera::toward`), snap `yaw` to the current yaw rounded to the nearest 90° and evaluate `basis_right`'s pole guard at that yaw (`right = (-sin yaw, cos yaw, 0)`) instead of literal +X; roll stays stable per chosen yaw, and a new pin demands the post-click on-screen up within 45° of the pre-click up. The two current view_cube_tests pins (`toward_turns_the_eye_without_moving_it`, `pole_views_hold_a_stable_roll`) get re-pinned with a `docs/decisions/` rationale.\n",
